{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120418","id":3895035745,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7oKYdh","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120418","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120418.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120418.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120418","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120418/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120418/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120418/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d7d7baee8a04069e969fbe71ee144da832dd6ff3","number":120418,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix growth directions not being respected when resizing `Control` nodes","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #120167\r\n- Closes #120345 \r\n\r\nFor the longest time, growth direction applied only to minimum size changes for some reason, resulting in some peculiar behavior when resizing them normally.\r\nIf the size was changed before the anchors were set, all would be good. Flip that process and all of a sudden, the child `Control` would go from nicely fitting within the parent, to being completely over the edge:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"86\" height=\"89\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed51bbd2-c48a-4c7a-ae06-97ec99275820\" />\r\n<img width=\"153\" height=\"143\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27506a9f-4981-433c-9865-0fbd9e0db154\" />\r\n\r\nUsing RTL would also make it worse, resulting in it being over the edge with the \"end\" growth anchor (default), but not the \"begin\" one.\r\n\r\nWith this fix, changing the size of a `Control` will correctly account for growth direction, which means both paths end with the same result: your child is the size you want it, where you want it.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAll comparisons follow the same flow:\r\n0. Start with `Panel` of size `50,50`\r\n1. Set the anchor mode\r\n2. Set layout direction (RTL or LTR/Standard)\r\n3. Set the new size to `100,100`\r\n\r\nScreenshots have the parent `Control` selected, which is the default from \"User Interface\" scene creation (i.e., a viewport-sized `Control` using \"Full Rect\" anchor mode).\r\n\r\n| Anchor | Layout Direction | Before | After |\r\n| -- | -- | -- | -- |\r\n| top-left | LTR | <img width=\"151\" height=\"153\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7ca0f42c-53bc-40cc-bc97-03ae04a13f64\" /> | <img width=\"149\" height=\"153\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f201458b-9496-4920-99b0-31565de3eadb\" /> |\r\n| top-left | RTL | <img width=\"134\" height=\"137\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9d5118d-6850-46cc-852f-58a0bcffcef3\" /> | <img width=\"147\" height=\"157\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fd93cf54-aa59-4dbc-94fc-9653a7e00746\" /> |\r\n| bottom-right | LTR | <img width=\"139\" height=\"135\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/816cb533-a12a-4480-a295-b4e2be6c4e5a\" /> | <img width=\"142\" height=\"141\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f843bcc-e933-4f05-8f44-59f3bb2e1431\" /> |\r\n| bottom-right | RTL | <img width=\"163\" height=\"135\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dcef0d67-50f7-47e1-85cb-1dc96e44503e\" /> | <img width=\"161\" height=\"147\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e94f315-0c2c-4daa-bc80-f49547903f62\" /> | ","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.g